      "claim": "Polar rigid molecules isosorbide-5-mononitrate and topiramate show high oral bioavailability (82–93% and >80%), so high TPSA and low logD alone do not establish F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C18", "C25", "C42", "C22"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Lefamulin, a polycyclic diterpene, shows absolute oral bioavailability of 24–26% in fasted subjects, above the threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C06", "C38", "C59", "C77"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No transferable context provides affirmative measured evidence of F < 20%; the low tacrolimus rat formulation values are species/formulation-specific and not applicable to this polar rigid polycyclic lactone.",
      "card_ids": ["C46", "C55", "C65", "C74", "C75"]
    }
  ],
