    "Transferability is inferred from structural similarity and measured outcomes in related contexts, not from a matched query experiment.",
    "The low prior is descriptor-based and not supported by measured threshold-relevant evidence.",
    "Tacrolimus rat low values are not transferable due species and formulation differences."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The descriptor-based low prior is uncertain and not affirmative. L1 and L2 records across transferable contexts—dihydroartemisinin (45–85%), digitoxin (~90%), isosorbide-5-mononitrate (82–93%), topiramate (>80%), and lefamulin (24–26%)—support F ≥ 20%. The only sub-20% values are tacrolimus rat formulations, which are not transferable to this polar rigid polycyclic lactone. Therefore high is better supported, with moderate confidence."
}

